(function(){
  try {
    if (typeof QB === 'undefined' || !Array.isArray(QB)) { if(window.console) console.warn('[qbank-ac] QB no disponible'); return; }
    window.QB_AC = [{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-COND-001","es":{"q":"¿Cuántas zonas de temperatura controla de forma independiente el aire acondicionado y cuáles son?","keys":["cockpit","cabin","sistema","totalmente","automatico","mantiene"],"answer":"El sistema es totalmente automático y mantiene una temperatura constante seleccionada en TRES zonas controladas de forma independiente: COCKPIT, FWD CABIN y AFT CABIN. Proporciona renovación continua del aire. La regulación fina de cada zona se logra añadiendo aire caliente con las trim air valves. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Tres: COCKPIT, FWD CABIN y AFT CABIN","Dos: cabina de vuelo y cabina de pasaje","Cuatro: cockpit, fwd, mid y aft","Una sola zona común a todo el avión"]},"en":{"q":"How many temperature zones does the air conditioning control independently, and which are they?","keys":["three","cockpit","cabin","system","fully","automatic"],"answer":"The system is fully automatic and maintains a constant selected temperature in THREE independently-controlled zones: COCKPIT, FWD CABIN and AFT CABIN. It provides continuous air renewal. Fine per-zone regulation is achieved by adding hot air through the trim air valves. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Three: COCKPIT, FWD CABIN and AFT CABIN","Two: flight deck and passenger cabin","Four: cockpit, fwd, mid and aft","A single zone common to the whole aircraft"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-COND-002","es":{"q":"¿Cómo se suministra el aire al sistema de acondicionamiento?","keys":["sistema","neumatico","pack","control","valves","packs"],"answer":"El aire lo suministra el sistema neumático a través de dos pack flow control valves, dos packs y la mixing unit (que mezcla el aire de los packs con el recirculado de cabina). En emergencia, un ram air inlet aporta aire ambiente a la mezcladora. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Por el sistema neumático, vía dos pack flow control valves, dos packs y la unidad mezcladora","Directamente de los compresores de motor, sin packs","Por ventiladores eléctricos que toman aire de cabina","Sólo por el APU en todas las fases"]},"en":{"q":"How is air supplied to the air conditioning system?","keys":["pneumatic","system","pack","control","valves","packs"],"answer":"Air is supplied by the pneumatic system through two pack flow control valves, two packs and the mixing unit (which mixes pack air with recirculated cabin air). In an emergency, a ram air inlet provides ambient air to the mixer. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["By the pneumatic system, via two pack flow control valves, two packs and the mixing unit","Directly from the engine compressors, without packs","By electric fans drawing cabin air","Only by the APU in all phases"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-001","es":{"q":"¿Qué función cumple la mixing unit (unidad mezcladora)?","keys":["mezcla","packs","cabina","recirculado","recirculation","mixing"],"answer":"La mixing unit mezcla el aire frío fresco de los packs con el aire de cabina recirculado por los recirculation fans. También está conectada al emergency ram air inlet y a las tomas de tierra de baja presión. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Mezcla el aire frío de los packs con el aire de cabina recirculado por los recirculation fans","Comprime el aire antes de los packs","Regula la presión de cabina","Separa el agua del aire antes de la turbina"]},"en":{"q":"What is the function of the mixing unit?","keys":["mixes","pack","cabin","recirculated","recirculation","mixing"],"answer":"The mixing unit mixes cold fresh pack air with cabin air recirculated through the recirculation fans. It is also connected to the emergency ram air inlet and the low-pressure ground inlets. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Mixes cold pack air with cabin air recirculated by the recirculation fans","Compresses air before the packs","Regulates cabin pressure","Separates water from the air before the turbine"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CTL-001","es":{"q":"En el panel AIR COND, ¿qué temperatura selecciona el zone temperature selector en posición de las 12 en punto?","keys":["24","selector","12","punto","corresponde","76"],"answer":"El selector de zona en las 12 en punto corresponde a 24 °C (76 °F). La posición COLD es 18 °C (64 °F) y la posición HOT es 30 °C (86 °F). El rango de selección va de 18 a 30 °C. (FCOM DSC-21-10-50 · p. 27 · rev 12 MAY 23)","opts":["24 °C","18 °C","30 °C","21 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the AIR COND panel, what temperature does the zone temperature selector set at the 12 o'clock position?","keys":["24","selector","12","clock","corresponds","76"],"answer":"The zone selector at 12 o'clock corresponds to 24 °C (76 °F). The COLD position is 18 °C (64 °F) and the HOT position is 30 °C (86 °F). The selection range is 18 to 30 °C. (FCOM DSC-21-10-50 · p. 27 · rev 12 MAY 23)","opts":["24 °C","18 °C","30 °C","21 °C"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-002","es":{"q":"Sobre la pack flow control valve, ¿qué afirmación es correcta?","keys":["accionamiento","neumatico","control","electrico","presion","resorte"],"answer":"La pack flow control valve es de accionamiento neumático y control eléctrico; regula el caudal según los pack controllers o la ACSC. Sin presión de aire, un resorte la mantiene CERRADA. Se cierra automáticamente ante pack overheat (sólo en tierra), arranque de motor, o fire/ditching pb. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 24 AUG 18)","opts":["Es de accionamiento neumático y control eléctrico; sin presión de aire un resorte la mantiene cerrada","Es de accionamiento eléctrico y control neumático","Permanece abierta por resorte si falta presión","La controla directamente el piloto con una palanca mecánica"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the pack flow control valve, which statement is correct?","keys":["pneumatically","operated","electrically","controlled","without","pressure"],"answer":"The pack flow control valve is pneumatically-operated and electrically-controlled; it regulates flow per the pack controllers or ACSC. Without air pressure, a spring holds it CLOSED. It closes automatically on pack overheat (on ground only), engine start, or the fire/ditching pb. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 24 AUG 18)","opts":["It is pneumatically-operated and electrically-controlled; without air pressure a spring holds it closed","It is electrically-operated and pneumatically-controlled","It is spring-held open if pressure is lost","It is directly controlled by the pilot with a mechanical lever"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-003","es":{"q":"¿Para qué sirve el emergency ram air inlet y cómo se acciona?","keys":["ventila","cockpit","cabina","eliminar","fallan","ambos"],"answer":"El emergency ram air inlet ventila cockpit y cabina para eliminar humo, o si fallan ambos packs. Se abre con el RAM AIR pb del panel AIR COND, siempre que no esté seleccionado ditching. Aporta aire ambiente a la mixing unit. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["Ventila cockpit y cabina para eliminar humo, o si fallan ambos packs; se abre con el RAM AIR pb (si ditching no está seleccionado)","Refrigera la aviónica en vuelo normal","Presuriza la cabina si fallan los CPC","Aporta bleed a los packs cuando el APU no está disponible"]},"en":{"q":"What is the emergency ram air inlet for, and how is it operated?","keys":["ventilates","cockpit","cabin","remove","smoke","packs"],"answer":"The emergency ram air inlet ventilates cockpit and cabin to remove smoke, or if both packs fail. It is opened with the RAM AIR pb on the AIR COND panel, provided ditching is not selected. It supplies ambient air to the mixing unit. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["Ventilates cockpit and cabin to remove smoke, or if both packs fail; opened with the RAM AIR pb (if ditching not selected)","Cools the avionics in normal flight","Pressurizes the cabin if the CPCs fail","Supplies bleed to the packs when the APU is unavailable"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-004","es":{"q":"¿Qué regula la hot-air pressure-regulating valve y desde dónde se controla?","keys":["presion","caliente","tomado","aguas","arriba","packs"],"answer":"La hot-air pressure-regulating valve regula la presión del aire caliente tomado aguas arriba de los packs, que alimenta las trim air valves. Es de accionamiento neumático y control eléctrico desde el HOT AIR pb; la regula la ACSC 1. Sin aire, un resorte la mantiene cerrada. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["La presión del aire caliente tomado aguas arriba de los packs; se controla con el HOT AIR pb (la regula la ACSC 1)","El caudal de los packs, desde el PACK FLOW selector","La presión de cabina, desde el MODE SEL","La temperatura del separador de agua"]},"en":{"q":"What does the hot-air pressure-regulating valve regulate, and how is it controlled?","keys":["pressure","tapped","upstream","packs","controlled","regulated"],"answer":"The hot-air pressure-regulating valve regulates the pressure of hot air tapped upstream of the packs, which feeds the trim air valves. It is pneumatically-operated and electrically-controlled from the HOT AIR pb; ACSC 1 regulates it. Without air, a spring keeps it closed. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["The pressure of hot air tapped upstream of the packs; controlled by the HOT AIR pb (regulated by ACSC 1)","The pack flow, from the PACK FLOW selector","The cabin pressure, from the MODE SEL","The water separator temperature"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CTL-002","es":{"q":"Al seleccionar el HOT AIR pb en OFF, ¿qué ocurre?","keys":["valve","cierra","valves","cierran","resetea","circuito"],"answer":"Con el HOT AIR pb en OFF, la hot air valve se cierra Y las trim air valves se cierran, y se resetea el circuito FAULT. En ON, la válvula regula la presión de aire caliente para la regulación fina de temperatura por zonas. (FCOM DSC-21-10-50 · p. 27 · rev 12 MAY 23)","opts":["La hot air valve se cierra y las trim air valves se cierran","Sólo se cierra la hot air valve; las trim air quedan abiertas","Se abre el emergency ram air","Se aumenta el caudal de los packs"]},"en":{"q":"When the HOT AIR pb is selected OFF, what happens?","keys":["valve","closes","valves","close","fault","circuit"],"answer":"With the HOT AIR pb OFF, the hot air valve closes AND the trim air valves close, and the FAULT circuit is reset. With ON, the valve regulates hot-air pressure for fine per-zone temperature control. (FCOM DSC-21-10-50 · p. 27 · rev 12 MAY 23)","opts":["The hot air valve closes and the trim air valves close","Only the hot air valve closes; the trim air valves stay open","The emergency ram air opens","Pack flow is increased"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-REG-001","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es el rango de selección de temperatura de las zonas?","keys":["18","30","rango","seleccion","temperatura","64"],"answer":"El rango de selección de temperatura va de 18 °C (64 °F) a 30 °C (86 °F). Con la posición central del selector en 24 °C. La tripulación de cabina puede afinar cada zona desde el FAP con autoridad limitada. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["18 °C a 30 °C","16 °C a 28 °C","20 °C a 26 °C","15 °C a 32 °C"]},"en":{"q":"What is the temperature selection range for the zones?","keys":["18","30","temperature","selection","range","64"],"answer":"The temperature selection range is 18 °C (64 °F) to 30 °C (86 °F), with the selector's central position at 24 °C. The cabin crew can fine-tune each zone from the FAP with limited authority. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["18 °C to 30 °C","16 °C to 28 °C","20 °C to 26 °C","15 °C to 32 °C"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-REG-002","es":{"q":"Desde el temperature control panel del FAP, ¿con qué autoridad puede la tripulación de cabina modificar la temperatura de cada zona durante el crucero?","keys":["respecto","seleccionado","cockpit","tripulacion","cabina","temperature"],"answer":"La tripulación de cabina, desde el temperature control panel del FAP, puede modificar cada zona de cabina seleccionada desde el cockpit con una autoridad LIMITADA de ± 2.5 °C (± 4.5 °F). No es autoridad total: la referencia la sigue fijando el cockpit. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["± 2.5 °C respecto a lo seleccionado en el cockpit","Autoridad total, sobreescribiendo la selección del cockpit","± 5 °C","No pueden modificarla, sólo el cockpit"]},"en":{"q":"From the FAP temperature control panel, with what authority can the cabin crew modify each zone temperature in cruise?","keys":["relative","cockpit","selection","fap","temperature","control"],"answer":"From the FAP temperature control panel, the cabin crew can modify each cabin zone selected from the cockpit with a LIMITED authority of ± 2.5 °C (± 4.5 °F). It is not full authority: the cockpit still sets the reference. (FCOM DSC-21-10-10 · p. 9 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["± 2.5 °C relative to the cockpit selection","Full authority, overriding the cockpit selection","± 5 °C","They cannot modify it, only the cockpit can"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-005","es":{"q":"En un pack, ¿cómo se enfría el aire (air cycle machine)?","keys":["intercambiador","primario","comprime","compresor","vuelve","enfriar"],"answer":"El bleed pre-acondicionado entra por la pack flow control valve al intercambiador primario, luego al compresor del air-cycle machine (sube presión y temperatura), se vuelve a enfriar en el intercambiador principal y entra en la turbina, donde se expande y genera potencia para mover el compresor y el cooling air fan. La expansión baja mucho la temperatura. Un water separator seca el aire antes de la turbina. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 15 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El aire pasa por un intercambiador primario, se comprime en el compresor del ACM, se vuelve a enfriar en el intercambiador principal y se expande en la turbina, que mueve compresor y ventilador","Sólo por intercambiadores de calor, sin partes móviles","Se enfría con un ciclo de refrigerante tipo aire acondicionado doméstico","Se mezcla con aire frío exterior directamente"]},"en":{"q":"In a pack, how is the air cooled (air cycle machine)?","keys":["passes","primary","exchanger","compressed","compressor","cooled"],"answer":"Pre-conditioned bleed enters via the pack flow control valve to the primary heat exchanger, then the air-cycle machine compressor (raising pressure and temperature), is cooled again in the main heat exchanger and enters the turbine, where it expands generating power to drive the compressor and cooling air fan. Expansion greatly lowers temperature. A water separator dries the air before the turbine. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 15 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Air passes a primary heat exchanger, is compressed in the ACM compressor, cooled again in the main heat exchanger and expanded in the turbine, which drives the compressor and fan","Only by heat exchangers, with no moving parts","It is cooled with a refrigerant cycle like a domestic air conditioner","It is mixed directly with cold outside air"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-REG-003","es":{"q":"¿Quién regula la temperatura y dónde se miden las temperaturas reales de referencia?","keys":["controller","acsc","cockpit","propio","sensor","cabina"],"answer":"La regulación la hace el zone controller o la ACSC. La temperatura real se mide con sensores: en el cockpit para la zona de cockpit; y en el circuito de extracción de lavabos y de ventilación de galleys para la cabina. La demanda más baja de zona se envía al pack controller/ACSC, que ajusta ambos packs. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El zone controller (o la ACSC): cockpit por su propio sensor; la cabina por los sensores del circuito de extracción de lavabos y de ventilación de galleys","Sólo los packs, con sensores en cada pack","El piloto manualmente, sin sensores","La mixing unit, con un sensor a la salida"]},"en":{"q":"What regulates temperature, and where are the actual reference temperatures measured?","keys":["controller","acsc","cockpit","sensor","cabin","sensors"],"answer":"Regulation is done by the zone controller or the ACSC. Actual temperature is measured by sensors: in the cockpit for the cockpit zone; and in the lavatory extraction circuit and galley ventilation system for the cabin. The lowest zone demand goes to the pack controller/ACSC, which adjusts both packs. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The zone controller (or ACSC): cockpit by its own sensor; the cabin by sensors in the lavatory extraction circuit and galley ventilation system","Only the packs, with sensors in each pack","The pilot manually, without sensors","The mixing unit, with a sensor at its outlet"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-006","es":{"q":"¿En cuál de estas situaciones NO se cierra automáticamente la pack flow control valve?","keys":["descenso","normal","ambos","motores","marcha","pack"],"answer":"La pack flow control valve se cierra automáticamente ante: pack overheat (sólo en tierra), arranque de motor, o accionamiento del fire pb o del ditching pb. En un descenso normal con motores en marcha permanece abierta y regulando caudal. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 24 AUG 18)","opts":["Descenso normal con ambos motores en marcha","Pack overheat en tierra","Arranque de motor","Operación del fire pb o del ditching pb"]},"en":{"q":"In which of these situations does the pack flow control valve NOT close automatically?","keys":["normal","descent","engines","running","pack","control"],"answer":"The pack flow control valve closes automatically on: pack overheat (on ground only), engine start, or operation of the fire pb or ditching pb. In a normal descent with engines running it stays open and regulating flow. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 24 AUG 18)","opts":["Normal descent with both engines running","Pack overheat on ground","Engine start","Operation of the fire pb or ditching pb"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-REG-004","es":{"q":"Independientemente de lo que seleccione la tripulación en el pack flow, ¿cuándo entrega el sistema un caudal MAYOR de forma automática?","keys":["operacion","pack","suministra","bleed","seleccion","sistema"],"answer":"Sea cual sea la selección del pack flow, el sistema entrega caudal MAYOR en operación con un solo pack, o cuando el APU suministra bleed air. Y entrega caudal normal si se selecciona LO/ECON pero la demanda de temperatura no puede satisfacerse. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["En operación con un solo pack, o cuando el APU suministra bleed","Nunca: el caudal es fijo según la selección","Sólo por encima de FL300","Cuando la temperatura de cabina está en el valor seleccionado"]},"en":{"q":"Whatever the crew selects for pack flow, when does the system automatically deliver HIGHER flow?","keys":["single","pack","operation","supplying","bleed","whatever"],"answer":"Whatever the crew selects, the system delivers HIGHER flow in single-pack operation, or when the APU is supplying bleed air. It also delivers normal flow if LO/ECON is selected but the temperature demand cannot be satisfied. (FCOM DSC-21-10-30 · p. 21 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["In single-pack operation, or when the APU is supplying bleed","Never: flow is fixed by the selection","Only above FL300","When cabin temperature is at the selected value"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-FLT-001","es":{"q":"Cada controlador del aire acondicionado tiene dos lanes. ¿Qué ocurre si falla el lane activo?","keys":["asume","control","completo","efecto","operativo","controlador"],"answer":"Cada controlador tiene dos lanes: uno controla y el otro asume el control completo si el activo falla. El fallo de UN lane no tiene efecto (el segundo lane toma el control). Sólo el fallo de AMBOS lanes provoca la pérdida del pack y el cierre de la hot air valve. (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["El otro lane asume el control completo, sin efecto operativo","Se pierde el pack asociado","Se cierra la hot air valve","Ambos packs se apagan"]},"en":{"q":"Each air conditioning controller has two lanes. What happens if the active lane fails?","keys":["other","takes","control","operational","effect","controller"],"answer":"Each controller has two lanes: one controls, the other takes over full control if the active one fails. A ONE-lane failure has no effect (the second lane takes over). Only a BOTH-lanes failure causes loss of the pack and closure of the hot air valve. (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The other lane takes over full control, with no operational effect","The associated pack is lost","The hot air valve closes","Both packs shut down"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-FLT-002","es":{"q":"Si la hot-air pressure-regulating valve falla CERRADA, ¿cómo queda la regulación de temperatura?","keys":["pierde","regulacion","optima","valves","cerrado","pack"],"answer":"Fallo abierta: sin efecto. Fallo CERRADA: se pierde la regulación optimizada, las trim air valves van a la posición totalmente cerrada, y entonces el pack 1 controla la temperatura del cockpit al valor seleccionado, mientras el pack 2 controla la cabina (FWD y AFT) a la MEDIA de las temperaturas seleccionadas. (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Se pierde la regulación óptima; las trim air valves van a cerrado; el pack 1 controla el cockpit al valor seleccionado y el pack 2 controla la cabina (FWD y AFT) a la media de las temperaturas seleccionadas","Sin efecto: la regulación óptima se mantiene","Ambos packs se apagan","La cabina pasa a control manual del piloto"]},"en":{"q":"If the hot-air pressure-regulating valve fails CLOSED, how does temperature regulation end up?","keys":["optimized","regulation","valves","fully","closed","pack"],"answer":"Failed open: no effect. Failed CLOSED: optimized regulation is lost, the trim air valves are driven fully closed, and then pack 1 controls cockpit temperature to the selected value while pack 2 controls the cabin (FWD and AFT) to the MEAN of the selected temperatures. (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Optimized regulation is lost; trim air valves go fully closed; pack 1 controls the cockpit to the selected value and pack 2 controls the cabin (FWD and AFT) to the mean of the selected temperatures","No effect: optimized regulation is maintained","Both packs shut down","The cabin reverts to manual pilot control"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-FLT-003","es":{"q":"Si falla el Air Cycle Machine (agarrotamiento de compresor/turbina), ¿cómo puede seguir operando el pack?","keys":["enfriamiento","intercambiador","exchanger","cooling","derivando","bypass"],"answer":"Con el ACM agarrotado, el pack puede operar en heat exchanger cooling mode: el aire enfriado en el intercambiador primario va directo aguas abajo de la turbina por la bypass valve. El agarrotamiento REDUCE el caudal del pack. La ACSC sigue regulando temperatura con bypass valve, ram air flap y trim air (menos caudal de aire caliente). (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["En modo de enfriamiento por intercambiador (heat exchanger cooling mode), derivando por la bypass valve; con caudal de pack reducido","El pack queda totalmente inoperativo","Con caudal aumentado para compensar","Sólo alimentando el cockpit"]},"en":{"q":"If the Air Cycle Machine fails (compressor/turbine seizure), how can the pack keep operating?","keys":["exchanger","cooling","bypassing","bypass","valve","reduced"],"answer":"With the ACM seized, the pack can operate in heat exchanger cooling mode: air cooled in the primary heat exchanger goes directly downstream of the turbine through the bypass valve. The seizure REDUCES pack flow. The ACSC still regulates temperature via the bypass valve, ram air flap and trim air (with less hot-air flow). (FCOM DSC-21-10-40 · p. 25 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["In heat exchanger cooling mode, bypassing via the bypass valve; with reduced pack flow","The pack is completely inoperative","With increased flow to compensate","Only supplying the cockpit"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-CMP-007","es":{"q":"Con el RAM AIR pb en ON, ¿qué condiciones se requieren para que la outflow valve se abra ~50 % y para que entre aire por el ram air?","keys":["outflow","valve","50","control","automatico","psi"],"answer":"Con RAM AIR ON: la outflow valve se abre ~50 % SÓLO si está bajo control automático y ΔP < 1 PSI (en manual no se abre sola, aunque ΔP < 1). Si ΔP > 1 PSI, la check valve situada aguas abajo del ram air door no abre aunque se seleccione el door, y no se suministra caudal. Por eso el ram air sólo es efectivo con la cabina prácticamente despresurizada. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["La outflow valve se abre ~50 % sólo bajo control AUTOMÁTICO y con ΔP < 1 PSI; si ΔP > 1 PSI, la check valve tras el ram air no abre y no hay caudal","La outflow valve se abre siempre al 50 %, en manual o auto","Basta con pulsar el RAM AIR, sin más condiciones","Sólo funciona por encima de 1 PSI de ΔP"]},"en":{"q":"With the RAM AIR pb ON, what conditions are required for the outflow valve to open ~50 % and for ram air to flow?","keys":["outflow","valve","opens","50","under","automatic"],"answer":"With RAM AIR ON: the outflow valve opens ~50 % ONLY under automatic control and ΔP < 1 PSI (in manual it does not auto-open, even if ΔP < 1). If ΔP > 1 PSI, the check valve downstream of the ram air door will not open even if the door is selected, and no flow is supplied. So ram air is only effective with the cabin essentially depressurized. (FCOM DSC-21-10-20 · p. 19 · rev 20 DEC 16)","opts":["The outflow valve opens ~50 % only under AUTOMATIC control and with ΔP < 1 PSI; if ΔP > 1 PSI, the check valve after the ram air will not open and there is no flow","The outflow valve always opens 50 %, in manual or auto","Just pressing RAM AIR is enough, no other conditions","It only works above 1 PSI of ΔP"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PRESS-001","es":{"q":"¿De qué componentes principales consta el sistema de presurización?","keys":["cpc","rpcu","outflow","valve","actuador","motores"],"answer":"El sistema consta de: dos Cabin Pressure Controllers (CPC), una Residual Pressure Control Unit (RPCU), una outflow valve con actuador de TRES motores (dos para automático, uno para manual), un panel de control y dos safety valves. Cualquiera de los tres motores puede accionar la outflow valve. (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Dos CPC, una RPCU, una outflow valve (actuador con 3 motores) y dos safety valves","Un CPC, una safety valve y una outflow valve","Dos outflow valves y dos CPC","Un CPC y dos safety valves, sin RPCU"]},"en":{"q":"What are the main components of the pressurization system?","keys":["rpcu","outflow","valve","actuator","motors","safety"],"answer":"The system consists of: two Cabin Pressure Controllers (CPC), one Residual Pressure Control Unit (RPCU), one outflow valve with a THREE-motor actuator (two automatic, one manual), one control panel and two safety valves. Any of the three motors can drive the outflow valve. (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Two CPCs, one RPCU, one outflow valve (actuator with 3 motors) and two safety valves","One CPC, one safety valve and one outflow valve","Two outflow valves and two CPCs","One CPC and two safety valves, no RPCU"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PRESS-002","es":{"q":"El sistema de presurización tiene cuatro funciones generales. ¿Cuál describe la PREPRESURIZACIÓN?","keys":["durante","despegue","presion","cabina","evitar","rotacion"],"answer":"Las cuatro funciones son: Ground (abre del todo la outflow valve en tierra), Prepresurización (durante el despegue sube la presión de cabina para evitar un surge de presión en la rotación), Presurización en vuelo (ajusta altitud y régimen de cabina) y Despresurización (tras la toma libera gradualmente la sobrepresión residual antes de que la función Ground abra del todo la outflow valve). (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Durante el despegue, sube la presión de cabina para evitar un pico de presión durante la rotación","Abre del todo la outflow valve en tierra","Libera la sobrepresión residual tras la toma","Ajusta la altitud de cabina en crucero"]},"en":{"q":"The pressurization system has four general functions. Which describes PREPRESSURIZATION?","keys":["during","takeoff","raises","cabin","pressure","avoid"],"answer":"The four functions are: Ground (fully opens the outflow valve on ground), Prepressurization (during takeoff raises cabin pressure to avoid a pressure surge at rotation), Pressurization in flight (adjusts cabin altitude and rate) and Depressurization (after touchdown gradually releases residual overpressure before the Ground function fully opens the outflow valve). (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["During takeoff, raises cabin pressure to avoid a pressure surge during rotation","Fully opens the outflow valve on ground","Releases residual overpressure after touchdown","Adjusts cabin altitude in cruise"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCMP-001","es":{"q":"Sobre los dos Cabin Pressure Controllers (CPC), ¿qué afirmación es correcta?","keys":["controladores","digitales","identicos","activo","standby","reciben"],"answer":"Los CPC son dos controladores digitales idénticos e independientes. En modo automático o semi-automático, uno está activo y el otro en standby. Reciben señales del ADIRS, FMGC, EIU y LGCIU, generan las señales para el ECAM y se comunican entre sí por un cross-channel link. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Son dos controladores digitales idénticos; en auto/semi-auto uno está activo y el otro en standby; reciben señales de ADIRS, FMGC, EIU y LGCIU","Trabajan siempre los dos a la vez en paralelo","Reciben señales sólo del FMGC","Son analógicos y no comunican entre sí"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the two Cabin Pressure Controllers (CPC), which statement is correct?","keys":["identical","digital","controllers","active","other","standby"],"answer":"The CPCs are two identical, independent digital controllers. In automatic or semi-automatic mode, one is active and the other on standby. They receive signals from ADIRS, FMGC, EIU and LGCIU, generate the ECAM signals, and communicate with each other via a cross-channel link. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["They are two identical digital controllers; in auto/semi-auto one is active and the other on standby; they receive signals from ADIRS, FMGC, EIU and LGCIU","Both always work together in parallel","They receive signals only from the FMGC","They are analogue and do not communicate with each other"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCMP-002","es":{"q":"¿Qué previenen las dos safety valves y con qué valores?","keys":["presion","cabina","demasiado","psi","ambiente","debajo"],"answer":"Las dos safety valves neumáticas independientes evitan que la presión de cabina suba demasiado (8.6 PSI sobre la ambiente) o baje demasiado (1 PSI por debajo de la ambiente). Están en el mamparo de presión trasero, por encima de la flotation line. En el ECAM, la indicación de safety valve abierta corresponde a ΔP indicada entre 8.2 y 8.9 PSI. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Que la presión de cabina sea demasiado alta (8.6 PSI sobre la ambiente) o demasiado baja (1 PSI por debajo de la ambiente)","Sólo la sobrepresión, a 9.0 PSI","Sólo la baja presión, a 2 PSI","La sobrepresión a 8.0 PSI y la baja presión a 0.5 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"What do the two safety valves prevent, and with what values?","keys":["cabin","pressure","going","psi","above","ambient"],"answer":"The two independent pneumatic safety valves prevent cabin pressure from going too high (8.6 PSI above ambient) or too low (1 PSI below ambient). They are on the rear pressure bulkhead, above the flotation line. On the ECAM, the safety-valve-open indication corresponds to an indicated ΔP between 8.2 and 8.9 PSI. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Cabin pressure from going too high (8.6 PSI above ambient) or too low (1 PSI below ambient)","Overpressure only, at 9.0 PSI","Underpressure only, at 2 PSI","Overpressure at 8.0 PSI and underpressure at 0.5 PSI"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCMP-003","es":{"q":"¿Dónde está situada la outflow valve y cuántos motores tiene su actuador?","keys":["derecho","fuselaje","bodega","carga","trasera","flotation"],"answer":"La outflow valve está en el lado derecho del fuselaje, detrás de la bodega de carga trasera y por debajo de la flotation line. Su actuador contiene tres motores: dos automáticos (cualquiera acciona la válvula en modo auto) y uno manual (para el modo manual). (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["En el lado derecho del fuselaje, tras la bodega de carga trasera y bajo la flotation line; su actuador tiene tres motores (dos automáticos, uno manual)","En el morro, con un motor","En el techo de cabina, con dos motores","En el mamparo de presión delantero, con cuatro motores"]},"en":{"q":"Where is the outflow valve located and how many motors does its actuator have?","keys":["right","fuselage","behind","cargo","compartment","below"],"answer":"The outflow valve is on the right-hand side of the fuselage, behind the aft cargo compartment and below the flotation line. Its actuator contains three motors: two automatic (either drives the valve in auto mode) and one manual (for manual mode). (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["On the right-hand side of the fuselage, behind the aft cargo compartment and below the flotation line; its actuator has three motors (two automatic, one manual)","In the nose, with one motor","In the cabin ceiling, with two motors","In the forward pressure bulkhead, with four motors"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PRESS-003","es":{"q":"En operación automática, ¿qué hace la tripulación y qué pasa si no hay datos del FMGS?","keys":["monitoriza","presion","sigue","perfiles","fmgs","datos"],"answer":"En automático la tripulación sólo monitoriza: la presión de cabina sigue los perfiles externos que el sistema recibe del FMGS. Si los datos del FMGS no están disponibles, la tripulación sólo necesita seleccionar la landing field elevation (con el LDG ELEV), que el sistema usa para sus perfiles internos. (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Sólo monitoriza; la presión sigue los perfiles del FMGS. Si no hay datos del FMGS, basta con seleccionar la landing field elevation","Controla activamente la outflow valve todo el vuelo","Debe seleccionar manualmente el régimen de cabina en cada fase","Nada: el sistema no usa datos externos"]},"en":{"q":"In automatic operation, what does the crew do, and what if FMGS data is unavailable?","keys":["monitors","pressure","follows","fmgs","schedules","unavailable"],"answer":"In automatic the crew only monitors: cabin pressure follows external schedules the system receives from the FMGS. If FMGS data is unavailable, the crew only needs to select the landing field elevation (with LDG ELEV), which the system uses for its internal schedules. (FCOM DSC-21-20-10 · p. 45 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Only monitors; pressure follows the FMGS schedules. If FMGS data is unavailable, the crew only needs to select the landing field elevation","Actively controls the outflow valve the whole flight","Must manually select the cabin rate in each phase","Nothing: the system uses no external data"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-001","es":{"q":"¿A qué altitud de cabina limita el controlador durante el crucero y hasta qué presión de campo apoya operaciones en aeropuertos altos?","keys":["000","crucero","optimizado","14","500","tierra"],"answer":"El controlador limita la altitud de cabina a aproximadamente 8 000 ft máximo durante el modo CRUISE, y está optimizado para apoyar operaciones en aeropuertos altos hasta una presión de 14 500 ft durante tierra, subida y descenso. Si la landing elevation supera 8 000 ft, la altitud de cabina se sube a 8 000 ft en crucero. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["Máx 8 000 ft en crucero; optimizado hasta 14 500 ft en tierra/subida/descenso","Máx 6 000 ft en crucero; hasta 10 000 ft en tierra","Máx 10 000 ft en crucero; hasta 8 000 ft en tierra","Sin límite en crucero"]},"en":{"q":"To what cabin altitude does the controller limit during cruise, and up to what field pressure does it support high-airfield operations?","keys":["000","cruise","optimized","14","500","ground"],"answer":"The controller limits cabin altitude to approximately 8 000 ft maximum during CRUISE mode, and is optimized to support high-airfield operations up to a pressure of 14 500 ft during ground, climb and descent phases. If landing elevation exceeds 8 000 ft, cabin altitude is raised to 8 000 ft in cruise. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["Max 8 000 ft in cruise; optimized up to 14 500 ft on ground/climb/descent","Max 6 000 ft in cruise; up to 10 000 ft on ground","Max 10 000 ft in cruise; up to 8 000 ft on ground","No limit in cruise"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-002","es":{"q":"En modo GROUND, ¿cuándo abre del todo la outflow valve tras el aterrizaje y a qué régimen se libera la presión residual en la toma?","keys":["55","despues","aterrizaje","presion","residual","500"],"answer":"En modo GROUND, antes del despegue y 55 s después del aterrizaje, la outflow valve abre del todo para asegurar que no queda presión residual de cabina. En la toma, cualquier presión residual se libera a un régimen vertical de cabina de 500 ft/min. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["55 s después del aterrizaje; presión residual a 500 ft/min","Inmediatamente al tocar; a 2 000 ft/min","70 s después; a 350 ft/min","No abre hasta apagar motores"]},"en":{"q":"In GROUND mode, when does the outflow valve fully open after landing, and at what rate is residual pressure released at touchdown?","keys":["55","after","landing","residual","pressure","500"],"answer":"In GROUND mode, before takeoff and 55 s after landing, the outflow valve fully opens to ensure no residual cabin pressure. At touchdown, any remaining cabin pressure is released at a cabin vertical speed of 500 ft/min. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["55 s after landing; residual pressure at 500 ft/min","Immediately at touchdown; at 2 000 ft/min","70 s after; at 350 ft/min","It does not open until engines are shut down"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-003","es":{"q":"En modo TAKEOFF, ¿cómo prepresuriza el controlador el avión y por qué?","keys":["400","alcanza","psi","evitar","presion","rotacion"],"answer":"En modo TAKEOFF, para evitar un pico de presión en la rotación, el controlador prepresuriza el avión a un régimen de 400 ft/min hasta que la ΔP alcanza 0.1 PSI. Al despegar (liftoff), el controlador inicia la fase de subida (CLIMB). (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["A 400 ft/min hasta que ΔP alcanza 0.1 PSI, para evitar un pico de presión en la rotación","A 500 ft/min hasta 1 PSI, para acelerar la subida","Despresurizando por completo antes del despegue","A 350 ft/min hasta 8 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"In TAKEOFF mode, how does the controller pre-pressurize the aircraft, and why?","keys":["400","until","reaches","psi","avoid","pressure"],"answer":"In TAKEOFF mode, to avoid a pressure surge at rotation, the controller pre-pressurizes the aircraft at 400 ft/min until ΔP reaches 0.1 PSI. At liftoff, the controller initiates the CLIMB phase. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["At 400 ft/min until ΔP reaches 0.1 PSI, to avoid a pressure surge at rotation","At 500 ft/min up to 1 PSI, to speed up the climb","Fully depressurizing before takeoff","At 350 ft/min up to 8 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCMP-004","es":{"q":"¿Qué hace la Residual Pressure Control Unit (RPCU) y bajo qué condiciones actúa?","keys":["despresuriza","automaticamente","tierra","abriendo","outflow","valve"],"answer":"La RPCU despresuriza automáticamente el avión ante presión residual anómala en tierra. Abre la outflow valve cuando se cumplen a la vez: la outflow valve no está del todo abierta; ambos CPC han fallado O se ha seleccionado modo manual; el avión está en tierra; y todos los motores están parados O todos los ADIRS indican velocidad inferior a 100 kt. Es la red de seguridad contra quedar presurizado en tierra. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Despresuriza automáticamente en tierra abriendo la outflow valve si: la válvula no está del todo abierta, ambos CPC fallan o hay modo manual, el avión está en tierra, y todos los motores parados o todos los ADIRS indican velocidad < 100 kt","Controla la presión de cabina en crucero","Abre las safety valves en vuelo","Cierra la outflow valve para el ditching"]},"en":{"q":"What does the Residual Pressure Control Unit (RPCU) do, and under what conditions?","keys":["automatically","depressurizes","ground","opening","outflow","valve"],"answer":"The RPCU automatically depressurizes the aircraft on abnormal residual ground pressure. It opens the outflow valve when all hold: the outflow valve is not fully open; both CPCs failed OR manual mode selected; the aircraft is on ground; and all engines shut down OR all ADIRS indicate speed below 100 kt. It is the safety net against staying pressurized on ground. (FCOM DSC-21-20-20 · p. 49 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Automatically depressurizes on ground by opening the outflow valve if: the valve is not fully open, both CPCs failed or manual mode, the aircraft is on ground, and all engines shut down or all ADIRS indicate speed < 100 kt","Controls cabin pressure in cruise","Opens the safety valves in flight","Closes the outflow valve for ditching"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-004","es":{"q":"Con dos sistemas automáticos de presurización, ¿cuándo se produce una transferencia automática de sistema?","keys":["70","despues","aterrizaje","falla","sistema","operando"],"answer":"Sólo un controlador opera a la vez. La transferencia automática al otro sistema ocurre 70 s después de cada aterrizaje, o si falla el sistema que está operando. Además, seleccionar MODE SEL en MAN durante al menos 10 s y volver a AUTO también selecciona el otro sistema. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["70 s después de cada aterrizaje, o si falla el sistema que está operando","Cada 30 min en crucero","Sólo si el piloto lo pide","Nunca; el mismo sistema controla todo el vuelo"]},"en":{"q":"With two automatic pressurization systems, when does an automatic system transfer occur?","keys":["70","after","landing","operating","system","fails"],"answer":"Only one controller operates at a time. Automatic transfer to the other system occurs 70 s after each landing, or if the operating system fails. Also, selecting MODE SEL to MAN for at least 10 s and back to AUTO selects the other system. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["70 s after each landing, or if the operating system fails","Every 30 min in cruise","Only if the pilot requests it","Never; the same system controls the whole flight"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-005","es":{"q":"Si fallan ambos sistemas automáticos, ¿cómo toma la tripulación el control manual de la presurización?","keys":["suelta","seleccionar","subir","bajar","altitud","cabina"],"answer":"Con ambos sistemas automáticos fallidos, la tripulación suelta el MODE SEL pb para seleccionar MAN y empuja el MAN V/S CTL UP o DN para subir o bajar la altitud de cabina. La primera acción corta la alimentación a los motores AUTO y habilita el motor MAN. La outflow valve NO abre automáticamente en la toma bajo control manual. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Suelta el MODE SEL pb para seleccionar MAN y usa el MAN V/S CTL (UP/DN) para subir/bajar la altitud de cabina","Tira del LDG ELEV a una posición fija","Pulsa el DITCHING pb","Apaga los packs"]},"en":{"q":"If both automatic systems fail, how does the crew take manual control of pressurization?","keys":["releases","select","raise","lower","cabin","altitude"],"answer":"With both automatic systems failed, the crew releases the MODE SEL pb to select MAN and pushes the MAN V/S CTL UP or DN to raise or lower cabin altitude. The first action cuts power to the AUTO motors and enables the MAN motor. In manual control the outflow valve does NOT open automatically at touchdown. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["Releases the MODE SEL pb to select MAN and uses the MAN V/S CTL (UP/DN) to raise/lower cabin altitude","Pulls the LDG ELEV to a fixed position","Presses the DITCHING pb","Switches the packs off"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-006","es":{"q":"En modo manual de presurización, ¿qué particularidad importante hay que recordar respecto a la toma?","keys":["outflow","valve","automaticamente","abrirla","manualmente","presurizacion"],"answer":"Como la presurización está bajo control manual, la outflow valve NO abre automáticamente en la toma. La tripulación debe gestionarla con el MAN V/S CTL. Además, por la lentitud del motor manual y la resolución limitada del ECAM, la indicación visual de un cambio de posición de la outflow valve puede tardar hasta 5 s. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["La outflow valve NO abre automáticamente en la toma: hay que abrirla manualmente","La outflow valve abre automáticamente al tocar, como en auto","Las safety valves abren solas al tocar","El sistema vuelve solo a AUTO al tocar"]},"en":{"q":"In manual pressurization mode, what important particularity must be remembered about touchdown?","keys":["outflow","valve","automatically","touchdown","opened","manually"],"answer":"Because pressurization is under manual control, the outflow valve does NOT open automatically at touchdown. The crew must manage it with the MAN V/S CTL. Also, due to the slow manual motor and limited ECAM resolution, the visual indication of an outflow valve position change can take up to 5 s. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The outflow valve does NOT open automatically at touchdown: it must be opened manually","The outflow valve auto-opens at touchdown, like in auto","The safety valves open by themselves at touchdown","The system reverts to AUTO by itself at touchdown"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-POPS-007","es":{"q":"Al pulsar el DITCHING pb, ¿qué válvulas cierra el sistema?","keys":["outflow","valve","emergency","ram","inlet","valvulas"],"answer":"El DITCHING pb envía una señal de cierre a: la outflow valve, el emergency ram air inlet, las válvulas de admisión y extracción de la ventilación de aviónica, las pack flow control valves y la FWD cargo outlet isolation valve. Así se cierran todas las aberturas bajo la flotation line. Nota: la outflow valve no cierra sola si está en control manual. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["La outflow valve, el emergency ram air inlet, las válvulas de admisión/extracción de ventilación de aviónica, las pack flow control valves y la FWD cargo outlet isolation valve","Sólo la outflow valve","Sólo los packs","Las safety valves"]},"en":{"q":"When the DITCHING pb is pressed, which valves does the system close?","keys":["outflow","valve","emergency","ram","inlet","avionics"],"answer":"The DITCHING pb sends a close signal to: the outflow valve, the emergency ram air inlet, the avionics ventilation inlet and extract valves, the pack flow control valves and the FWD cargo outlet isolation valve. This closes all openings below the flotation line. Note: the outflow valve won't close by itself under manual control. (FCOM DSC-21-20-30 · p. 51 · rev 21 MAR 16)","opts":["The outflow valve, the emergency ram air inlet, the avionics ventilation inlet and extract valves, the pack flow control valves, and the FWD cargo outlet isolation valve","Only the outflow valve","Only the packs","The safety valves"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCTL-001","es":{"q":"El LDG ELEV knob en AUTO, ¿qué hace?","keys":["sistema","datos","fmgs","construir","perfil","presion"],"answer":"En AUTO, el sistema usa los datos del FMGS para construir un perfil de presión optimizado. Para salir de AUTO hay que tirar del selector y girarlo; entonces el sistema usa la landing elevation seleccionada con el knob (de -2 000 a +14 000 ft) en vez de la del FMGS. La escala del knob es sólo orientativa: usar el ECAM para ajuste preciso. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 07 MAY 13)","opts":["El sistema usa los datos del FMGS para construir un perfil de presión optimizado","Fija la altitud de cabina en 8 000 ft","Selecciona el modo manual","Abre la outflow valve"]},"en":{"q":"What does the LDG ELEV knob do in AUTO?","keys":["system","fmgs","build","optimized","pressure","schedule"],"answer":"In AUTO, the system uses FMGS data to build an optimized pressure schedule. To exit AUTO, pull and turn the selector; then the system uses the landing elevation selected with the knob (from -2 000 to +14 000 ft) instead of the FMGS value. The knob scale is only indicative: use the ECAM for precise adjustment. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 07 MAY 13)","opts":["The system uses FMGS data to build an optimized pressure schedule","Fixes cabin altitude at 8 000 ft","Selects manual mode","Opens the outflow valve"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCTL-002","es":{"q":"¿Cómo se puede forzar el cambio al OTRO sistema de presurización con el MODE SEL pb?","keys":["seleccionando","durante","10","volviendolo","conmutar","devolverlo"],"answer":"Conmutar el MODE SEL pb a MAN durante al menos 10 s y devolverlo a AUTO selecciona el otro sistema de presurización. Es un truco útil si se sospecha del sistema activo. La FAULT (ámbar) del MODE SEL sólo se enciende cuando AMBOS sistemas automáticos están averiados. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["Seleccionando MODE SEL en MAN durante al menos 10 s y volviéndolo a AUTO","Pulsando el DITCHING pb","Tirando del LDG ELEV","No se puede: la transferencia sólo es automática tras el aterrizaje"]},"en":{"q":"How can you force a switch to the OTHER pressurization system with the MODE SEL pb?","keys":["selecting","least","10","returning","switching","selects"],"answer":"Switching the MODE SEL pb to MAN for at least 10 s and returning it to AUTO selects the other pressurization system. It is a useful trick if the active system is suspect. The MODE SEL FAULT (amber) comes on only when BOTH automatic systems are faulty. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["By selecting MODE SEL to MAN for at least 10 s and returning it to AUTO","By pressing the DITCHING pb","By pulling the LDG ELEV","It cannot be done: transfer is only automatic after landing"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCTL-003","es":{"q":"En la página ECAM CAB PRESS, ¿a qué régimen empieza a parpadear la indicación de CABIN VERTICAL SPEED?","keys":["750","parpadear","volver","debajo","650","indicacion"],"answer":"La indicación de CABIN VERTICAL SPEED parpadea cuando el régimen vertical de cabina alcanza 1 750 ft/min y deja de parpadear al volver por debajo de 1 650 ft/min. Es una alerta de que la cabina está cambiando de altitud demasiado rápido. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["A 1 750 ft/min (deja de parpadear al volver por debajo de 1 650 ft/min)","A 1 000 ft/min","A 500 ft/min","A 2 500 ft/min"]},"en":{"q":"On the ECAM CAB PRESS page, at what rate does the CABIN VERTICAL SPEED indication start flashing?","keys":["750","stops","flashing","returning","below","650"],"answer":"The CABIN VERTICAL SPEED indication flashes when the cabin vertical speed reaches 1 750 ft/min and stops flashing when returning below 1 650 ft/min. It warns that the cabin is changing altitude too fast. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["At 1 750 ft/min (stops flashing when returning below 1 650 ft/min)","At 1 000 ft/min","At 500 ft/min","At 2 500 ft/min"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-PCTL-004","es":{"q":"En la página ECAM CAB PRESS, la indicación de CABIN ALTITUDE parpadea a 8 800 ft. ¿A qué valor pasa a ámbar (aviso de altitud de cabina alta)?","keys":["550","altitud","encima","indicacion","cabin","altitude"],"answer":"La indicación de CABIN ALTITUDE parpadea al alcanzar 8 800 ft (deja de parpadear por debajo de 8 600 ft) y pasa a ámbar cuando la altitud de cabina está a 9 550 ft o por encima. Ese es el umbral asociado a la alerta de altitud de cabina excesiva. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["A 9 550 ft (a esa altitud o por encima)","A 8 000 ft","A 10 000 ft","A 14 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the ECAM CAB PRESS page, CABIN ALTITUDE flashes at 8 800 ft. At what value does it turn amber (high cabin altitude warning)?","keys":["550","above","altitude","cabin","indication","flashes"],"answer":"The CABIN ALTITUDE indication flashes on reaching 8 800 ft (stops below 8 600 ft) and turns amber when cabin altitude is at or above 9 550 ft. That is the threshold associated with the excess cabin altitude warning. (FCOM DSC-21-20-40 · p. 57 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["At 9 550 ft (at or above that altitude)","At 8 000 ft","At 10 000 ft","At 14 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-VENT-001","es":{"q":"¿Qué cubre el sistema de ventilación?","keys":["avionica","controlada","aevc","baterias","lavabos","galleys"],"answer":"El sistema de ventilación incluye la ventilación de: la aviónica (controlada por el Avionics Equipment Ventilation Computer, AEVC), las baterías, y los lavabos y galleys. La ventilación de la carga se trata aparte (DSC-21-40). (FCOM DSC-21-30-10 · p. 69 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["La aviónica (controlada por el AEVC), las baterías, y los lavabos y galleys","Sólo la aviónica","Sólo la cabina de pasaje","Sólo los lavabos"]},"en":{"q":"What does the ventilation system cover?","keys":["avionics","controlled","aevc","batteries","lavatories","galleys"],"answer":"The ventilation system includes ventilation for: the avionics (controlled by the Avionics Equipment Ventilation Computer, AEVC), the batteries, and the lavatories and galleys. Cargo ventilation is covered separately in DSC-21-40, so it is not part of this general ventilation description. (FCOM DSC-21-30-10 · p. 69 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["The avionics (controlled by the AEVC), the batteries, and the lavatories and galleys","Only the avionics","Only the passenger cabin","Only the lavatories"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-VENT-002","es":{"q":"Sobre la ventilación de aviónica, ¿qué afirmación es correcta?","keys":["totalmente","automatica","ventiladores","electricos","refrigera","avionica"],"answer":"La ventilación de aviónica es totalmente automática. Refrigera los componentes eléctricos y electrónicos del compartimento de aviónica y de la cabina de vuelo (incluidos los paneles de instrumentos y de circuit breakers), usando dos ventiladores eléctricos. Parte del aire se aspira desde el cockpit a través de los distintos paneles. (FCOM DSC-21-30-20 · p. 71 · rev 24 FEB 11)","opts":["Es totalmente automática, usa dos ventiladores eléctricos y refrigera la aviónica y la cabina de vuelo (incluidos paneles de instrumentos y de circuit breakers)","Es manual y la controla el piloto","Sólo funciona en tierra","Sólo refrigera la cabina de pasaje"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding avionics ventilation, which statement is correct?","keys":["fully","automatic","electric","cools","avionics","flight"],"answer":"Avionics ventilation is fully automatic. It cools the electrical and electronic components in the avionics compartment and on the flight deck (including instrument and circuit breaker panels), using two electric fans. Part of the air is drawn from the cockpit through the various panels. (FCOM DSC-21-30-20 · p. 71 · rev 24 FEB 11)","opts":["It is fully automatic, uses two electric fans and cools the avionics and the flight deck (including instrument and circuit breaker panels)","It is manual and controlled by the pilot","It only works on ground","It only cools the passenger cabin"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"GEN","kid":"K-AC-VENT-003","es":{"q":"El Fan Speed Controller (FSC) regula la velocidad de los ventiladores de aviónica según la temperatura. ¿Cuándo van a velocidad alta?","keys":["temperatura","ventilacion","supera","40","velocidad","debajo"],"answer":"Los dos ventiladores circulan aire de forma continua siempre que el avión tenga alimentación eléctrica. El FSC pone velocidad ALTA cuando la temperatura del aire de ventilación supera +40 °C (104 °F), y velocidad BAJA cuando baja de +35 °C (95 °F). (FCOM DSC-21-30-20 · p. 71 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Cuando la temperatura del aire de ventilación supera +40 °C (baja velocidad por debajo de +35 °C)","Siempre a velocidad alta","Cuando la temperatura del aire de ventilación baja de +35 °C","La velocidad la fija el piloto"]},"en":{"q":"The Fan Speed Controller (FSC) sets avionics fan speed by temperature. When do they run at high speed?","keys":["ventilation","temperature","above","40","speed","below"],"answer":"The two fans continuously circulate air whenever the aircraft is electrically supplied. The FSC sets HIGH speed when the ventilation air temperature is above +40 °C (104 °F), and LOW speed when it drops below +35 °C (95 °F). (FCOM DSC-21-30-20 · p. 71 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["When the ventilation air temperature is above +40 °C (low speed below +35 °C)","Always at high speed","When the ventilation air temperature drops below +35 °C","Fan speed is set by the pilot"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EXCAB-001","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, si la alerta CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT se dispara POR ENCIMA de FL 160, ¿qué debe hacer la tripulación?","keys":["aplicar","primero","memory","items","descent","luego"],"answer":"Si el CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT se dispara por encima de FL 160, la tripulación debe aplicar PRIMERO los memory items del EMER DESCENT y después el procedimiento ECAM (cuyos primeros pasos recuerdan los memory items). Por debajo de FL 160, en cambio, se aplica el ECAM y se inicia un descenso normal. (FCTM PR-AEP-CAB_PR · p. 425 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Aplicar primero los memory items del EMER DESCENT y luego el procedimiento ECAM","Aplicar sólo el procedimiento ECAM sin descender","Continuar a nivel esperando a que la cabina se estabilice","Iniciar un descenso normal sin memory items"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, if the CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT alert triggers ABOVE FL 160, what should the crew do?","keys":["first","apply","descent","memory","items","perform"],"answer":"If CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT triggers above FL 160, the crew must FIRST apply the EMER DESCENT memory items and then perform the ECAM procedure (whose first steps recall the memory items). Below FL 160, instead, apply the ECAM and initiate a normal descent. (FCTM PR-AEP-CAB_PR · p. 425 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["First apply the EMER DESCENT memory items and then perform the ECAM procedure","Apply only the ECAM procedure without descending","Continue level waiting for the cabin to stabilize","Initiate a normal descent without memory items"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EXCAB-002","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, si el CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT se dispara POR DEBAJO de FL 160, ¿qué se hace?","keys":["aplicar","procedimiento","ecam","iniciar","descenso","normal"],"answer":"Por debajo de FL 160, la tripulación aplica el procedimiento ECAM e inicia un descenso NORMAL (no de emergencia). La distinción con FL 160 marca si se lanzan los memory items del EMER DESCENT (por encima) o basta el ECAM con descenso normal (por debajo). (FCTM PR-AEP-CAB_PR · p. 425 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Aplicar el procedimiento ECAM e iniciar un descenso normal","Aplicar los memory items del EMER DESCENT y descenso de emergencia","Nada, es una alerta espuria por debajo de FL 160","Ascender para reducir la ΔP"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, if CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT triggers BELOW FL 160, what is done?","keys":["apply","ecam","procedure","initiate","normal","descent"],"answer":"Below FL 160, the crew applies the ECAM procedure and initiates a NORMAL descent (not an emergency one). The FL 160 split determines whether the EMER DESCENT memory items are used (above) or the ECAM with a normal descent suffices (below). (FCTM PR-AEP-CAB_PR · p. 425 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Apply the ECAM procedure and initiate a normal descent","Apply the EMER DESCENT memory items and an emergency descent","Nothing, it is a spurious alert below FL 160","Climb to reduce ΔP"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EMERD-001","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, ¿en qué basa la tripulación la identificación de un evento de despresurización para iniciar un EMER DESCENT?","keys":["cualquiera","altitud","regimen","cabina","excesivos","controlables"],"answer":"La tripulación identifica la despresurización por cualquiera de: una altitud de cabina y régimen de ascenso excesivos y no controlables; el disparo del CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT; o la caída de TODAS las máscaras de oxígeno en cabina (por un presostato independiente). Por decisión de la tripulación, un EMER DESCENT puede iniciarse por cualquier otra urgencia. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["En cualquiera de: altitud/régimen de cabina excesivos y no controlables, la alerta CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT, o la caída de TODAS las máscaras de oxígeno de cabina","Sólo en el CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT","Sólo en la caída de las máscaras de oxígeno","Sólo en una altitud de cabina alta"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, on what does the crew base identification of a depressurization event to initiate an EMER DESCENT?","keys":["excessive","uncontrollable","cabin","altitude","excess","alert"],"answer":"The crew identifies depressurization by any of: excessive and uncontrollable cabin altitude and rate of climb; triggering of CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT; or ALL cabin oxygen masks dropping (via an independent pressure switch). By crew decision, an EMER DESCENT may be initiated for any other urgency. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["On any of: excessive and uncontrollable cabin altitude/rate, the CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT alert, or ALL cabin oxygen masks dropping","Only on CAB PR EXCESS CAB ALT","Only on the oxygen masks dropping","Only on a high cabin altitude"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EMERD-002","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, en el EMER DESCENT a niveles altos, ¿por qué hay que vigilar la VLS al extender los speed brakes?","keys":["evitar","activar","proteccion","angulo","ataque","retraeria"],"answer":"En el EMER DESCENT se recomienda usar AP y A/THR. A niveles altos se extienden los speed brakes vigilando la VLS, para evitar activar la protección de alto ángulo de ataque, que provocaría la retracción de los speed brakes y la desconexión del AP. Con IDLE, alta velocidad y speed brakes, el régimen de descenso es de ~7 000 ft/min. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Para evitar activar la protección de ángulo de ataque, que retraería los speed brakes y desconectaría el AP","Para no superar la VMO","Porque los speed brakes no funcionan por encima de FL300","Para mantener la presurización"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, in an EMER DESCENT at high levels, why must VLS be monitored when extending the speed brakes?","keys":["avoid","triggering","angle","attack","protection","would"],"answer":"In the EMER DESCENT, AP and A/THR use is recommended. At high levels the speed brakes are extended while monitoring VLS, to avoid triggering the high angle-of-attack protection, which would retract the speed brakes and disconnect the AP. At IDLE, high speed with speed brakes, the descent rate is ~7 000 ft/min. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["To avoid triggering the angle-of-attack protection, which would retract the speed brakes and disconnect the AP","To avoid exceeding VMO","Because speed brakes don't work above FL300","To maintain pressurization"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EMERD-003","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, durante un EMER DESCENT, ¿cuándo debe pulsar la tripulación el MASK MAN ON pb?","keys":["altitud","cabina","supera","14","000","pueden"],"answer":"Si la altitud de cabina supera 14 000 ft, la tripulación DEBE pulsar el MASK MAN ON pb. Si es evidente que la superará, pueden pulsarlo antes de alcanzar 14 000 ft. Además, el TCAS se mantiene en TA/RA (la evitación de colisión tiene prioridad, incluso interrumpiendo temporalmente el descenso). (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Si la altitud de cabina supera 14 000 ft (pueden anticiparlo si es evidente que la superará)","Nunca; las máscaras funcionan solas","Sólo tras aterrizar","Al pasar FL 100"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, during an EMER DESCENT, when must the crew press the MASK MAN ON pb?","keys":["cabin","altitude","above","14","000","anticipate"],"answer":"If cabin altitude goes above 14 000 ft, the crew MUST press the MASK MAN ON pb. If it is obvious it will exceed it, they may press it before reaching 14 000 ft. Also, TCAS stays on TA/RA (collision avoidance has priority, even temporarily interrupting the descent). (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["If cabin altitude goes above 14 000 ft (they may anticipate it if it is obvious it will exceed)","Never; the masks work by themselves","Only after landing","When passing FL 100"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EMERD-004","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, si durante la despresurización se sospecha daño estructural (un fuerte estruendo o un régimen vertical de cabina muy alto), ¿qué debe hacer la tripulación?","keys":["poner","speed","aumentar","reducirla","brakes","cuidado"],"answer":"Si se sospecha daño estructural (fuerte estruendo o régimen vertical de cabina muy alto), la tripulación debe: poner el SPEED/MACH pb en SPEED, para evitar que aumente la IAS o para reducirla (minimiza el estrés sobre la estructura); y usar los speed brakes con cuidado, para no añadir estrés adicional a la estructura. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Poner el SPEED/MACH pb en SPEED (para no aumentar la IAS, o reducirla) y usar los speed brakes con cuidado, minimizando el estrés estructural","Aumentar la velocidad para descender antes","Extender todo el speed brake de golpe","Mantener Mach constante y no tocar la velocidad"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, if structural damage is suspected during depressurization (a loud bang or a very high cabin vertical speed), what should the crew do?","keys":["speed","avoid","increasing","reduce","brakes","carefully"],"answer":"If structural damage is suspected (loud bang or very high cabin vertical speed), the crew must: set the SPEED/MACH pb to SPEED, to prevent an IAS increase or to reduce it (minimizing stress on the structure); and use the speed brakes carefully, to avoid additional stress on the structure. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Set the SPEED/MACH pb to SPEED (to avoid increasing IAS, or to reduce it) and use the speed brakes carefully, minimizing structural stress","Increase speed to descend sooner","Fully extend the speed brakes at once","Keep Mach constant and not touch the speed"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"ABN","kid":"K-AC-EMERD-005","es":{"q":"Según el FCTM, tras un descenso de emergencia y por debajo de FL 100, ¿a qué debe limitarse el régimen de descenso (salvo en aproximación) y en qué modo se mantiene el TCAS?","keys":["000","tcas","debajo","100","tripulacion","limitar"],"answer":"Por debajo de FL 100, la tripulación debe limitar el régimen de descenso a aproximadamente 1 000 ft/min, salvo durante la fase de aproximación. Durante todo el proceso, el selector de TCAS se mantiene en TA/RA: la evitación de colisión tiene prioridad, incluso si obliga a interrumpir temporalmente el descenso. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["A ~1 000 ft/min; TCAS en TA/RA","A 3 000 ft/min; TCAS en TA only","Sin límite; TCAS en STBY","A ~500 ft/min; TCAS off"]},"en":{"q":"Per the FCTM, after an emergency descent and below FL 100, to what should the descent rate be limited (except on approach), and in which mode is TCAS kept?","keys":["000","tcas","below","100","should","limit"],"answer":"Below FL 100, the crew should limit the descent rate to approximately 1 000 ft/min, except during the approach phase. Throughout, the TCAS selector stays on TA/RA: collision avoidance has priority, even if it requires temporarily interrupting the descent. (FCTM PR-AEP-MISC · p. 479 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["To ~1 000 ft/min; TCAS in TA/RA","To 3 000 ft/min; TCAS in TA only","No limit; TCAS in STBY","To ~500 ft/min; TCAS off"]}}];
    QB.push.apply(QB, window.QB_AC);
    if(window.console) console.log('[qbank-ac] +' + window.QB_AC.length + ' preguntas AIR/PRESS/VENT bilingües');
  } catch (e) { if (window.console) console.warn('[qbank-ac] no se pudo enganchar al QB:', e); }
})();
